the best stuff I've ever written...


00:21:51.877 --> 00:21:54.846
...because it's got this naive idealism thing
going on...


00:21:55.013 --> 00:21:58.005
...where ours is gonna be
the greatest love stories ever told.


00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.844
And I'm writing it.


00:22:00.652 --> 00:22:02.745
So I'm sitting there reading these emails...


00:22:03.188 --> 00:22:05.247
...and there's some turbulence...


00:22:05.424 --> 00:22:08.951
...and I start to have
this massive panic attack.


00:22:09.127 --> 00:22:10.992
Like nothing I've ever had.


00:22:11.229 --> 00:22:14.528
And I think it's happening...


00:22:14.699 --> 00:22:19.568
...because I can not imagine ever feeling
that way about anybody else ever again.


00:22:19.738 --> 00:22:23.071
Listen, I have never, in my life,
received anything...


00:22:23.241 --> 00:22:25.505
...like the kind of letters you wrote her.


00:22:25.677 --> 00:22:27.907
Never written one, either.


00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:30.504
And you're lucky. You're lucky in a way...


00:22:30.682 --> 00:22:33.207
...that has nothing to do
with this particular girl.


00:22:33.385 --> 00:22:34.784
But you already know that.


00:22:35.787 --> 00:22:37.982
I must sound so young to you.


00:22:38.156 --> 00:22:40.716
Yeah, well, screw you, pal.


00:22:40.892 --> 00:22:43.520
Come on. I didn't mean it like that.


00:22:43.695 --> 00:22:45.458
I know what you meant.


00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:48.258
You know, I pride myself
on being this great listener...


00:22:48.433 --> 00:22:52.130
...but whenever I meet somebody new,
I find I'm doing all the talking.


00:22:52.304 --> 00:22:53.498
What is that?


00:22:54.339 --> 00:22:56.899
Maybe you're not really
such a great listener.


00:22:57.375 --> 00:23:00.674
Maybe you're not such a great listener.


00:23:00.846 --> 00:23:04.213
No. No, that's not it.
I'm a great listener.


00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:08.248
Yeah, but that's the thing.
I hear myself talking about it.


00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:10.980
Nelson's career. Lucy's painting.


00:23:11.156 --> 00:23:14.922
Like they're my own interests and
my own accomplishments, but they're not.


00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:19.820
And I find myself wondering,
"Where am I? What am I?"


00:23:19.998 --> 00:23:21.590
Let me ask you this.


00:23:21.766 --> 00:23:24.826
Like, what is it exactly you do
with your days?


00:23:25.604 --> 00:23:27.595
You see, now, that is just so predictable.


00:23:27.772 --> 00:23:31.572
There is the perception that because
I don't have a job or I'm not in school...


00:23:31.743 --> 00:23:34.735
...that I'm sitting around doing nothing,
which is ridiculous.


00:23:34.913 --> 00:23:38.144
Most days I don't have
five seconds to myself.


00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:42.613
I'm driving somebody around or dealing
with the house or making the meals.


00:23:42.787 --> 00:23:45.381
Not to mention I'm on, like, 15 boards.


00:23:45.557 --> 00:23:47.320
I'm sorry. I didn't think that... .


00:23:47.492 --> 00:23:51.292
Yeah, I know you didn't,
but my family does, you know?


00:23:51.463 --> 00:23:55.365
I can feel them all just silently judging.
Especially Lucy.


00:23:55.534 --> 00:23:57.365
No matter what I do, l-


00:23:57.536 --> 00:24:00.801
It's like I'm just disappointing to her.


00:24:00.972 --> 00:24:03.805
Well, she's a teenager.
You're her mother.


00:24:03.975 --> 00:24:06.808
I mean, it'd be weird
if she didn't feel that way, right?


00:24:07.546 --> 00:24:12.347
I don't know. I'm sorry,
I do think about it and so I'm touchy.


00:24:12.884 --> 00:24:14.545
But maybe I could be doing more.


00:24:14.719 --> 00:24:17.313
God, I just don't wanna
look back on my life...


00:24:19.391 --> 00:24:22.588
...and wonder what part of it
belonged to me.


00:24:23.261 --> 00:24:24.956
Okay.


00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.324
- Yeah.
- So--


00:24:26.498 --> 00:24:28.398
That was really nice. Thank you.


00:24:28.567 --> 00:24:33.903
Yeah, you're welcome. I mean,
it was really great to talk to you.


00:24:34.072 --> 00:24:36.506
- Yeah, all right.
- Okay.


00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:40.104
- Shit.
- What?


00:24:40.278 --> 00:24:42.371
- Shit.
- What?


00:24:44.015 --> 00:24:46.210
I'm a last-word freak.


00:24:47.018 --> 00:24:48.349
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:51.216
Okay, well, I'm gonna go inside.


00:24:51.389 --> 00:24:53.721
You just shout something to me
as I'm walking away.


00:24:53.892 --> 00:24:55.120
- That'd be great.
- Perfect.


00:24:55.293 --> 00:24:57.124
- Great.
- Okay.


00:25:00.899 --> 00:25:02.594
You're gonna be all right.


00:25:09.941 --> 00:25:13.206
I don't know. Do you maybe wanna
do this again? Like tomorrow or... .


00:25:14.579 --> 00:25:17.980
Oh, l-- Sorry, I can't tomorrow.
I have an appointment.


00:25:18.149 --> 00:25:20.049
Okay. All right.
Don't worry about it.


00:25:20.218 --> 00:25:23.278
- Wednesday?
- Yeah. That would be awesome.


00:25:23.455 --> 00:25:24.786
I'll come by.


00:25:24.956 --> 00:25:26.480
- Okay. Well, I guess--
- Carter.


00:25:39.704 --> 00:25:42.935
"Awesome"? That's... .


00:25:43.275 --> 00:25:46.267
Mom, I can't talk about this anymore.
It's too retarded.


00:25:46.444 --> 00:25:48.935
And I really do not wanna fight
with you right now.


00:25:49.114 --> 00:25:52.015
It's not a fight. It's not a fight.
It's not even a big deal.


00:25:52.183 --> 00:25:54.743
I'm just saying
he's basically alone over there.


00:25:54.919 --> 00:25:56.648
You could just take him to a movie.


00:25:56.821 --> 00:25:59.688
Do you have any idea
how lame that would sound?


00:26:00.558 --> 00:26:04.858
It would redefine lame. Seriously.
Are you ready to make history?


00:26:07.832 --> 00:26:09.527
She might have a point, sweetheart.


00:26:09.701 --> 00:26:12.534
It could be a little awkward.
What do we know about this guy?


00:26:12.704 --> 00:26:15.070
Forget it. Just forget it.


00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:18.676
I thought maybe, maybe, just do
something nice for somebody sometime...


00:26:18.843 --> 00:26:21.505
...but I can't handle the two of you
ganging up on me.


00:27:15.233 --> 00:27:17.565
This is happening
because we're all really scared.


00:27:17.736 --> 00:27:20.762
So I'm gonna say to you
the same thing I said to her.


00:27:20.939 --> 00:27:24.306
Whatever we find out tomorrow,
we deal with it together.


00:27:25.110 --> 00:27:27.305
Now, your daughter
would like to apologize...


00:27:27.479 --> 00:27:29.709
...and she said, if you really want her to...


00:27:29.881 --> 00:27:33.442
...she'll go across the street now
and ask Crazy's grandson out on a date.


00:27:33.618 --> 00:27:36.086
He's a sweet kid. I feel bad for him.


00:27:36.254 --> 00:27:39.348
He's heartsick.


00:27:43.661 --> 00:27:46.289
I'm gonna be with you every second.


00:28:05.617 --> 00:28:07.141
What?


00:28:08.153 --> 00:28:09.381
Well, I'm just curious.


00:28:09.554 --> 00:28:13.786
Do you ever worry that you're gonna
get stuck in one of those positions?


00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:18.122
Yes, I do.


00:28:19.497 --> 00:28:20.987
Ready for bed?


00:28:22.233 --> 00:28:24.895
Did you know yoga increases circulation...


00:28:25.069 --> 00:28:28.800
...promotes health and well-being
and also reduces anxiety?


00:28:28.973 --> 00:28:30.941
Yeah, I've read that.


00:28:31.476 --> 00:28:33.910
Well, maybe you could try it.


00:28:38.116 --> 00:28:40.983
Hey, you know what?


00:28:43.054 --> 00:28:48.253
I'm sorry if I've seemed
a little bit distracted lately.


00:28:49.694 --> 00:28:51.252
It's cool.


00:29:00.738 --> 00:29:02.399
Good night, muffin.


00:29:03.842 --> 00:29:05.673
Did you get my pills?


00:29:05.844 --> 00:29:09.109
Yeah, these are some pretty serious
tranquilizers you got here.


00:29:09.280 --> 00:29:12.875
Are you sure it's safe
to be taking these all at once?


00:29:17.889 --> 00:29:19.516
I love it.


00:29:28.466 --> 00:29:30.491
Who changed the sheets?


00:29:30.668 --> 00:29:32.135
I did.


00:29:46.150 --> 00:29:47.742
Who's Sofia?


00:29:49.821 --> 00:29:51.220
How did you know about that?


00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:54.483
Oh, you kind of mutter in your sleep.


00:29:54.659 --> 00:29:56.593
What are you doing in my room
when I'm sleeping?


00:29:56.761 --> 00:29:59.628
That's a really good question.


00:30:03.868 --> 00:30:05.995
Well, she was my girlfriend...


00:30:06.170 --> 00:30:08.695
...and she doesn't wanna
be with me anymore.


00:30:09.173 --> 00:30:10.834
Is she zaftig?


00:30:12.377 --> 00:30:14.811
Yeah. Spectacular, actually.


00:30:14.979 --> 00:30:17.504
That's so important.


00:30:56.788 --> 00:30:58.517
I'm Sofia.


00:31:01.459 --> 00:31:04.553
<i>I am completely in love with you.</i>


00:31:13.137 --> 00:31:14.399
Goodbye.


00:31:34.025 --> 00:31:35.686
Hey. How you doing?


00:31:39.364 --> 00:31:41.423
- Yes?
- Do you know where you are?


00:31:41.599 --> 00:31:44.159
I'm just regrouping.


00:31:48.439 --> 00:31:52.136
- I could give you a ride home if you want.
- No. I'm good.


00:31:52.310 --> 00:31:55.279
Gotta keep running. It's healthy.


00:32:16.501 --> 00:32:18.162
Actually, you know what?


00:32:20.505 --> 00:32:24.635
My mom and I kind of
got into this fight the other night.


00:32:24.809 --> 00:32:27.642
I mean, it wasn't really a fight,
it was just... .


00:32:27.812 --> 00:32:31.304
She wanted me to maybe ask you
if you wanted...


00:32:32.150 --> 00:32:33.742
...to go see a movie or something.


00:32:35.386 --> 00:32:37.911
And I told her
that it would be really embarrassing.


00:32:38.089 --> 00:32:40.489
It would be the last thing
that you'd want to do.


00:32:40.658 --> 00:32:45.288
I mean, some creepy girl accosting you
like you're some kind of charity.


00:32:45.730 --> 00:32:47.220
This is really coming out wrong.


00:32:47.398 --> 00:32:51.767
Your parents, they normally pretty cool
about letting you go out on a school night?


00:32:51.936 --> 00:32:53.062
Not really.


00:32:53.237 --> 00:32:56.536
Do you think if you were
taking me to a movie...


00:32:56.708 --> 00:32:59.199
...being neighborly,
they might make an exception?


00:33:00.578 --> 00:33:01.602
I don't know.


00:33:01.779 --> 00:33:04.441
All right. Find out. Get back to me.


00:33:14.559 --> 00:33:15.924
What is it?


00:33:16.227 --> 00:33:18.354
It's possible...


00:33:18.529 --> 00:33:21.293
...I think maybe...


00:33:21.966 --> 00:33:24.457
...my toilet might be stopped up.


00:33:24.635 --> 00:33:27.536
Maybe? What's the variable?


00:33:27.705 --> 00:33:30.697
Water's running over the top.


00:33:30.875 --> 00:33:32.866
The carpet's all wet.


00:33:33.811 --> 00:33:38.111
Well, I'll take a look. First, I just gotta
stop off in my room and kill myself.


00:33:55.099 --> 00:33:57.567
I think I should tell Paige alone.


00:33:57.735 --> 00:34:00.499
I think it's less scary
if it's coming from me...


00:34:00.671 --> 00:34:02.605
...and she sees that I'm fine.


00:34:03.074 --> 00:34:04.302
I think you're right.


00:34:05.409 --> 00:34:06.740
But I want you to tell Lucy.


00:34:12.617 --> 00:34:14.175
It's better that way.


00:34:14.752 --> 00:34:18.279
So he goes, "Find out. Get back to me."


00:34:18.456 --> 00:34:20.890
Which is not exactly like, whatever...


00:34:21.058 --> 00:34:23.891
...but it definitely indicates
that he might be, you know--


00:34:24.061 --> 00:34:26.757
- Interested?
- Yeah. Kind of, right?


00:34:26.931 --> 00:34:30.492
I mean, even if he were,
it would still be the most awkward--


00:34:30.668 --> 00:34:32.727
- Do it.
- You think?


00:34:32.904 --> 00:34:35.338
Yeah. You have to do it.
And you know what else?


00:34:35.506 --> 00:34:39.169
Like, seriously,
you have to take me with you.


00:34:47.418 --> 00:34:50.285
All right. Somebody better tell me
what's going on here.


00:34:51.923 --> 00:34:54.915
I really want ice cream.
I've been thinking about that all day.


00:34:55.092 --> 00:34:56.423
Who wants to come with me?


00:34:56.594 --> 00:34:58.858
Wait, but what--?


00:34:59.030 --> 00:35:00.725
You want me to go get ice cream?


00:35:03.100 --> 00:35:05.762
You know what? You two go ahead.


00:35:06.404 --> 00:35:09.999
Lucy and I are gonna take Bozo for a walk.
Come on. It'll be good.


00:35:19.383 --> 00:35:21.078
Does it hurt?


00:35:24.722 --> 00:35:26.087
No.


00:35:29.227 --> 00:35:33.288
The chemotherapy can be rough,
and they said there's nausea.


00:35:34.966 --> 00:35:37.025
And it could make me tired.


00:35:39.971 --> 00:35:41.802
Are you scared?


00:35:43.140 --> 00:35:45.233
Yeah, sometimes.


00:35:45.910 --> 00:35:49.812
Not right now, though.
Right now I feel pretty tough.


00:35:52.350 --> 00:35:54.318
You don't look so tough.


00:36:00.291 --> 00:36:02.122
I took $20 from your purse.


00:36:03.594 --> 00:36:05.118
Really? When?


00:36:05.997 --> 00:36:09.524
A while ago. Last February.


00:36:10.635 --> 00:36:12.000
Are you serious?


00:36:12.503 --> 00:36:13.936
Yeah.


00:36:15.539 --> 00:36:18.303
I've been wanting to tell you for a while.


00:36:18.776 --> 00:36:21.438
I felt bad about it. I'm sorry.


00:36:21.612 --> 00:36:25.378
Well, just out of curiosity,
what did you need $20 for?


00:36:26.017 --> 00:36:27.780
It's stupid.


00:36:28.352 --> 00:36:32.846
I wanted to start saving money,
you know, for the future.


00:36:34.825 --> 00:36:37.225
But I didn't have any money...


00:36:38.129 --> 00:36:40.063
...so I needed a foundation.


00:36:41.365 --> 00:36:44.357
Right. Well, at least
you're financially responsible.


00:36:46.904 --> 00:36:50.897
I'm telling you because other than that,
I don't have any secrets from you.


00:36:51.075 --> 00:36:54.476
- It's okay to keep some things to yourself.
- Yeah, but I don't.


00:36:54.645 --> 00:36:59.105
Like, I always tell you the truth
because you always tell me the truth.


00:36:59.283 --> 00:37:00.614
Right?


00:37:02.653 --> 00:37:04.314
Right.


00:37:04.722 --> 00:37:08.055
If you say everything's gonna be okay,
I believe you.


00:37:08.225 --> 00:37:11.388
And I know you're telling the truth
because you wouldn't lie to me.


00:37:12.263 --> 00:37:14.697
Maybe to other people...


00:37:15.866 --> 00:37:19.199
...like, maybe to Lucy
or maybe to Dad...


00:37:19.370 --> 00:37:21.031
...but not to me.


00:37:26.010 --> 00:37:28.205
I just needed to know.


00:37:31.048 --> 00:37:33.175
Are you gonna be okay?


00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:17.591
Hey.


00:38:21.165 --> 00:38:23.065
What's going on?


00:38:23.467 --> 00:38:26.402
You look good.
You look better than you did the other day.


00:38:36.514 --> 00:38:39.608
- So, what was her name?
- Sorry?


00:38:39.784 --> 00:38:43.515
- The girl you wrote all those letters to.
- Oh, Sofia.


00:38:45.289 --> 00:38:48.053
- Was she your first love?
- Yeah.


00:38:48.225 --> 00:38:50.216
Well, there was somebody
in high school...


00:38:50.394 --> 00:38:53.386
...but I used to have this tendency
to project onto girls...


00:38:53.564 --> 00:38:56.431
...my fantasies of what
I thought they should be like.


00:38:56.600 --> 00:38:59.569
Didn't have anything to do
with what they were actually like.


00:38:59.737 --> 00:39:02.205
It would just take me forever
to figure that out.


00:39:02.373 --> 00:39:04.773
Usually four to five months.


00:39:05.643 --> 00:39:07.440
But Sofia was different?


00:39:07.611 --> 00:39:09.977
Yeah. Well, you know.


00:39:12.950 --> 00:39:16.283
No. Actually, that was pretty much
the same deal.


00:39:17.588 --> 00:39:19.078
Well... .


00:39:20.991 --> 00:39:23.721
Come on.
There's something I wanna show you.


00:39:28.165 --> 00:39:31.566
This is exciting.
Do you know where we're going?


00:39:31.735 --> 00:39:35.171
<i>I feel like we're gonna
run into the cast of Deliverance.</i>


00:39:36.307 --> 00:39:37.899
Love it here.


00:39:39.176 --> 00:39:43.010
I have this whole science-fiction scenario
worked out...


00:39:43.948 --> 00:39:48.146
...where I pretend that since
there's no evidence of modern life...


00:39:48.319 --> 00:39:50.480
...that I could walk out of these woods...


00:39:50.654 --> 00:39:55.148
...and be in another time
and a different place.


00:39:55.326 --> 00:39:57.226
I love that.


00:40:08.973 --> 00:40:11.601
My husband has been having an affair.


00:40:13.511 --> 00:40:17.174
I found out a while ago
and I didn't do anything about it.


00:40:20.784 --> 00:40:24.743
I told myself
it's because of the girls and... .


00:40:29.126 --> 00:40:32.618
I just have a very comfortable life.
It's very clean.


00:40:33.097 --> 00:40:34.758
I'm good at that, you know?


00:40:36.634 --> 00:40:41.037
And the thing is, he's really a decent guy.
I mean, he's a good provider and... .


00:40:42.740 --> 00:40:46.870
Anyway, it's discreet, I guess.
I don't know.


00:40:47.678 --> 00:40:49.612
That must sound pretty vacant to you.


00:40:50.714 --> 00:40:55.117
I wouldn't even begin to know
how to have an opinion about that.


00:40:58.088 --> 00:41:00.147
The thing is, I just don't... .


00:41:00.524 --> 00:41:02.458
I just don't love him.


00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:05.790
Not like you love her.
Not like that kind of love...


00:41:05.963 --> 00:41:07.828
...where it hurts when it's good...


00:41:07.998 --> 00:41:10.228
...especially when it's good, you know?


00:41:11.902 --> 00:41:15.838
The further away I get from that
and the more I talk to you, you know...


00:41:16.173 --> 00:41:18.539
...l'm not so sure
that was real love either.


00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:26.174
You know, I'd really like
just to give you a hug right now.


00:41:26.350 --> 00:41:28.011
Would that be weird?


00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:54.637
Hey, Lucy can't know anything
about Nelson's--


00:41:54.812 --> 00:41:57.372
- Sarah.
- Right.


00:41:57.748 --> 00:41:59.579
Goes without saying.


00:42:00.117 --> 00:42:04.850
You know, she asked me about taking you
to a movie on a school night specifically.


00:42:05.022 --> 00:42:07.490
We usually don't let her
go out on the weekdays.


00:42:07.691 --> 00:42:10.216
That's responsible.


00:42:10.394 --> 00:42:11.986
I'm making an exception.


00:42:12.162 --> 00:42:14.153
I'm guessing tomorrow
you probably have... .


00:42:14.331 --> 00:42:17.459
Yeah. Another appointment.


00:42:18.602 --> 00:42:22.663
Hey, look, I don't know
when I'm gonna be able to do this again.


00:42:22.840 --> 00:42:26.674
It might be a couple days, might be longer.
I do have a lot of stuff coming up.


00:42:26.844 --> 00:42:28.277
All right.


00:42:30.047 --> 00:42:31.840
But I have to go to the grocery store.

